+# Changes: round 0
+
+## Added
+
+- `src/wrap.mjs`: exports `wrap(text, width)`. Greedy word wrap that breaks
+  only at whitespace, collapses runs of spaces/tabs to one space, trims each
+  paragraph, treats newlines (`\n` or `\r\n`) as paragraph boundaries, keeps a
+  blank line between paragraphs as exactly one blank line, drops leading and
+  trailing blank lines, and puts a single over-long word on its own line
+  unbroken. Throws `TypeError` for a non-string `text` or a `width` that is not
+  a positive integer. Same ESM + JSDoc style as `src/count.mjs`.
+- `tests/wrap.test.mjs`: `node:test` + `node:assert/strict` tests covering
+  every behaviour line in ACCEPTANCE.md (items 2 through 10), including
+  property-style checks that no line exceeds the width and that no line has
+  leading or trailing spaces across several inputs and widths.
+
+## Changed
+
+- `README.md`: added a short `wrap` usage example after the `countWords` one.
+
+## Unchanged
+
+- `package.json` (the existing `node --test tests/*.test.mjs` script picks up
+  the new test file), `src/count.mjs`, `tests/count.test.mjs`.
+
+## Interpretation notes
+
+- ACCEPTANCE.md item 8 says a blank line between paragraphs is preserved "as
+  one blank line" but does not say what several consecutive blank lines become.
+  `wrap` collapses any run of blank lines to a single blank line, in the same
+  spirit as item 7's whitespace collapsing. A blank line that contains only
+  spaces or tabs counts as blank.
+- `\r\n` is accepted as a newline so Windows input does not leave a stray `\r`
+  on the end of a paragraph. Not required by the acceptance file; harmless.
